{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars","id":489929,"title":"The Exalted related to the Lunars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-23T15:51:44-07:00","id":489929,"title":"The Exalted related to the Lunars","content":"THere was some comment about an unknown exalted type that was closely related to the lunars- but I can't find the comments on them. Does anyone have any links to those comments if any?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T15:56:57-07:00","id":489956,"title":"","content":"I think we got no info except that there are one or two new Exalted types that are especially relevant to, or foils to, Lunars in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T16:53:13-07:00","id":490058,"title":"","content":"Pure speculation: Possibly somebody more deeply embedded and invested in the marginal and the fringe societies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T16:53:51-07:00","id":490059,"title":"","content":"Yeah, information's been pretty sparse. We know that there are two new types of Exalted that can serve as foils to Lunars, and John implied that one or both belong to a new class* of Exalts. Thanks to the Great and Powerful Minton, I have links to summaries for each.<br /> <br /> * The meaning of &quot;class&quot; here is uncertain, though it reads to me as another in the vein of Celestial, Terrestrial, and Exigent.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2015/01/27/ask-the-developers-thread-summary-post-6/\" target=\"_blank\">Ask the Developers Summary Post 6</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there are two new types of Exalts for the Lunars, not just one.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://ericminton.wordpress.com/2015/03/07/ask-the-developers-thread-summary-post-9/\" target=\"_blank\">Ask the Developers Summary Post 9</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new class of Exalts that are tied to the Lunars are called the [REDACTED].</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":"caveat. 04-23-2015, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T16:56:16-07:00","id":490062,"title":"","content":"Hm. I dunno. I'd like to see Luthe developed more. Maybe something Cthulu-esque?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T17:31:06-07:00","id":490081,"title":"","content":"I think one should be careful not to read too much into incidental words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T17:37:51-07:00","id":490085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queshire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=490062#post490062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I dunno. I'd like to see Luthe developed more. Maybe something Cthulu-esque?</div> </div> </div> </div>Luthe would be much more interesting if it wasn't all about revenge/torture porn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=490081#post490081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one should be careful not to read too much into incidental words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:16:18-07:00","id":490101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=490081#post490081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one should be careful not to read too much into incidental words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, generally when I hear the word &quot;class&quot; used in Exalted it's not referring to categories in the fashion of &quot;Terrestrial, Celestial.&quot; Besides, Alchemicals, Abyssals, and Infernals don't really fit into that either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T19:05:07-07:00","id":490129,"title":"","content":"Eh, feels like it makes the most sense to me in context, but I'll add a caveat. As for Alchemicals, Abyssals, Infernals, and Liminals, that'd be part of the reason I specified &quot;known,&quot; as Terrestrial, Celestial, and Exigent are the only ones we presently know.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I will freely admit part of my thinking comes from the mention of the following, <a href=\"http://ericminton.wordpress.com/2015/03/07/ask-the-developers-thread-summary-post-9/\" target=\"_blank\">just a little before</a>. Whether the availability heuristic is accurate here or not isn't something I can know.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of \u201cExigent\u201d the way you think of \u201cCelestial.\u201d It\u2019s not one type of Exalt but many different types. The Exigent of a volcano god is very different from Strawmaiden Janest.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Availability heuristic jabber. 04-23-2015, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T21:07:42-07:00","id":490173,"title":"","content":"A new class you say?<br /> Presumably Solars, DBs and Lunars are the feudal class, Sidereals are petty-bourgeoisie, Alchemicals are either Feudal or Workers. So the new anti-Lunars must be proper bourgeoisie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T21:23:07-07:00","id":490181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=490173#post490173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A new class you say?<br /> Presumably Solars, DBs and Lunars are the feudal class, Sidereals are petty-bourgeoisie, Alchemicals are either Feudal or Workers. So the new anti-Lunars must be proper bourgeoisie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves fit into the feudal system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T21:26:21-07:00","id":490184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=490181#post490181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves fit into the feudal system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lycanthropes played an essential role in the development of the feudal <i>seisin </i>system, hence the modern property law term of a deed held &quot;in fee simple werewolf.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T00:46:54-07:00","id":490289,"title":"","content":"Lunars are the mates of Solars: Ladies to their Lords. A Lady may not hold any land, but she's still part of the Feudal class.<br /> Or, for a more direct example, there were tons of Feudal Werewolves: Bisclavret, Lycaon, Gorlagon, Vereticus. Also, there's a few real-life noblemen who were believed to be werewolves; Prince Usiaslau of Belarus, and Prince Vseleslav of Polotsk (those two might be the same person spelt different ways, I'm not sure), for example. Vseleslav was well known to be a werewolf, which caused his famous temper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":".  Edited for sub-par grammar. I spent all day teaching grammar, I think I'm grammared-out. 04-24-2015, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T02:32:30-07:00","id":490353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=490289#post490289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are the mates of Solars: Ladies to their Lords. A Lady may not hold any land, but she's still part of the Feudal class.<br /> Or, for a more direct example, there were tons of Feudal Werewolves: Bisclavret, Lycaon, Gorlagon, Vereticus. Also, there's a few real-life noblemen who were believed to be werewolves; Prince Usiaslau of Belarus, and Prince Vseleslav of Polotsk (those two might be the same person spelt different ways, I'm not sure), for example. Vseleslav was well known to be a werewolf, which caused his famous temper.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is in contrast to Britain/Canada's current royal bloodline, who actually ARE werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T09:17:12-07:00","id":490627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=490353#post490353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is in contrast to Britain/Canada's current royal bloodline, who actually ARE werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>But weren't werewolves just some kind of alien? In Exalted terms, would that make Werewolves Fair Folk?<br /> ...I try to make a joke, and it ends up making sense, given the Lunar/Wyld link of 2ed as well as the fact that Fair Folk can totally play werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T10:39:30-07:00","id":490701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=490184#post490184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lycanthropes played an essential role in the development of the feudal <i>seisin </i>system, hence the modern property law term of a deed held &quot;in fee simple werewolf.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is actually the basis for the common Realm title limitation, where deeds are often held in fee simple subject to executory sidereals. It's all part of Saturn's common-law formulation of the rule against perpetuities.*<br /> <br /> <br /> *she <i>really means it</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T12:18:47-07:00","id":490797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=490353#post490353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is in contrast to Britain/Canada's current royal bloodline, who actually ARE werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well obviously (though to be fair it's Britain/Canada/NZ/Australia/Jamaica/Barbados/Trinidad and Tobago's royal bloodline... I feel it's easier just to say British).<br /> And they do an excellent job defending Britain from banes, fomori, etc. Why, I don't know anyone who was murdered by Black Spiral Dancers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T12:39:50-07:00","id":490808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=490353#post490353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is in contrast to Britain/Canada's current royal bloodline, who actually ARE werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canada is <i>packed</i> with werewolves! Most of them are in Quebec though. Folklore has it that one who does not go to confession for 7 whole years is/becomes a werewolf.<br /> That might explain my monthly blackouts...<br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">I'm kidding of course. I remember everything.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-24-2015, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T15:56:21-07:00","id":491024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=490797#post490797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well obviously (though to be fair it's Britain/Canada/NZ/Australia/Jamaica/Barbados/Trinidad and Tobago's royal bloodline... I feel it's easier just to say British).<br /> And they do an excellent job defending Britain from banes, fomori, etc. Why, I don't know anyone who was murdered by Black Spiral Dancers.</div> </div> </div> </div>They must be empowered and united by a steady supply of beef chow mein and pina coladas, courtesy of London. Their hair is also perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T20:51:04-07:00","id":491234,"title":"","content":"Something gives me the distinct impression that in absence of any solid information this thread has veered so far off topic that it just beached itself on the sandy shores of another topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some Tunes for your Exalted Game? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071249-exalted-tunes\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-exalted-tunes</a><br /> Want some help managing your PCs? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882498-new-anathema-character-management-anathema-reincarnated\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-reincarnated</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","name":"Arian Dynas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T01:23:03-07:00","id":491443,"title":"","content":"I wonder if at least one of the complementary Exalted might be enemies, or at least competition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T05:19:42-07:00","id":491547,"title":"","content":"If there are two different kind of Exalts that are related to them, then I'd expect at least one type to be primarily antagonistic. The other, perhaps less so, more co-operative or at least, as you say, just competitive.<br /> <br /> Currently, the primary Exalted antagonist Exalts for Lunars are probably the Dragonblood. The Lunars and their barbarians in the threshold oppose the Realm satrapies.<br /> The issue, is that these are not antagonists who dwell on the same turf as the Lunars. Some Lunars do of course live in or infiltrate the satrapies, but the Dragonblood's power doesn't reach into the wildnerness, deserts and deep forests where the Lunars have their main strongholds and biggest influence.<br /> On the other hand, you have the Raksha out in the Wyld, clawing at the Lunars' domains. Again, some Lunars dwell in the Wyld, but it's not really their home turf.<br /> But these are border wars, not Exalt types that live alongside the Lunars.<br /> <br /> So an antagonist (or at least competitor) whose main environment is also the deep threshold would probably work best, without trampling over Lunar themes (I mean, if there was the &quot;animal Exalted&quot; as a stereotypical example, they'd have an obvious link with Lunars, but they'd be trampling over Lunar themes. Although Lunars live primarily in the deep threshold, and have a &quot;barbarian aesthetic&quot; that's not really their theme, you can still have a Lunar who lives in Chiaroscoro. So putting other Exalt types' power centres there puts them in competition with Lunars, but doesn't mean they're taking away thematic weight from the Lunars).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T14:47:18-07:00","id":491949,"title":"","content":"I wonder if one is Chosen of the Ishvara/Unshaped...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T15:46:34-07:00","id":492054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=491949#post491949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if one is Chosen of the Ishvara/Unshaped...</div> </div> </div> </div>Unshaped aren't really a thing anymore, but an Ishvara could certainly have the sort of power and metaphysical oomph necessary. It's also not impossible that some among the Fair Folk might be able to achieve the kind of power needed without reaching those heights.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I admit to having a wild guess that there may be some kind of new Exalt type with analogs to Changeling. Whether ultimately antagonistic to Lunars or not, I could see potential for them making good foils, perhaps in terms of Lunars emphasizing that which is physical and real, while these hypothetical fey-tied Exalts more play up dreams and the unreal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T16:25:40-07:00","id":492080,"title":"","content":"That would be an obvious idea, but it seems to me that it wouldn't add a lot to the game: you'd just be making a more human, more powerful Raksha, essentially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T17:54:13-07:00","id":492125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The new class of Exalts that are tied to the Lunars are called the [REDACTED]. </div> </div> </div>The trick here is that John is not redacting anything. Their name is genuinely the [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> (Actually, I think there have been hints that the [REDACTED] Exalted -- that is, the Exalted who would have &quot;[REDACTED]&quot; as a sobriquet -- are Getimians.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T22:03:30-07:00","id":492336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/489929-the-exalted-related-to-the-lunars?p=492080#post492080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be an obvious idea, but it seems to me that it wouldn't add a lot to the game: you'd just be making a more human, more powerful Raksha, essentially.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find that argument convincing. By that logic, Exigents wouldn't add a lot to the game: you'd just be making a more human, more powerful god, essentially. Just as there isn't some generic god, there isn't some generic Fair Folk: there's breadth there for the Chosen of a raksha to develop Charms rooted in the personal mythology her patron has built for herself over her lifetime. There's more than one way to tackle &quot;dreams and the unreal&quot; across two splats. I mean, Sidereals and Getimians are finding different spaces in which to riff on &quot;fate-associated supernatural martial artists,&quot; which feels like a much more narrow space to me.<br /> <br /> The raksha could also provide a fairly unique feel as patrons. They are the exiled remnants of a proud people brought low, trapped between the home to which they cannot return and a world they love and hate that is antithetical to them by its nature. If one of them elevates a mortal, there's going to be some inherent contention and friction there that could make for a very interesting relationship. It's not exactly a secret that the raksha find Creation-born souls to be delicacies beyond compare; even a Fair Folk who scrupulously avoids it, or certainly would with her own Chosen, is going to carry some low-level tension to their interactions.<br /> <br /> Here's one original (ish) take, off the top of my head: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">There are times when a Fair Folk finds itself trapped in Creation with little time left to it -- or all too much time. When dying to a wound or the cruel pressure of calcification (or from within the empty doldrums of existence as a reliquary), these princes of chaos will sometimes reach out to the dreams of mortals. Every once in a great while, such a one is lucky: it finds a mortal with vast dreams that resonate with the faerie's Heart, and beckon it in. Sometimes this raksha come with sweet lies or cruel truths, sometimes bearing bargains fair and foul, and sometimes simply surging through. Whatever the course, the raksha claims this mortal's soul as its place of respite from a too-harsh world. And this Dreamer finds a spark lit within her, one that blossoms into a full flower of the Wyld's majesty and possibility.<br /> <br /> Despite this power, the Dreamer's course is imperiled, as the injured and hungry Fair Folk can only exert so much control over its appetite. If the Exalt does not take care to nurture her dreams and keep this legend nourished, her guest will either feed on that which is human in her until only her dreams remain -- and then swallow even those -- or briefly loose itself on the world in a terrible, beautiful bedlam. Caught between a sleeping life now impossible to resume and the monster that dwells in her soul, the Dreamer wields Charms that draw on her guest's resonant narrative and the dreams that drew it in. She charts a course to bring those dreams into the real.</div> <br /> This would also echo that, &quot;good person with a monster inside or monster with a good person inside,&quot; remark John made about Lunars ages ago, so that's fun, too. ^_^</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T23:16:38-07:00","id":492373,"title":"","content":"People don't really play gods (and gods aren't really designed to be playable), but they do play Raksha.<br /> I see your point though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T00:15:17-07:00","id":492387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div c